# Routing, carried INSIDE the build output.
#
# Why this file exists and not only netlify.toml: setting `base` in the root
# netlify.toml makes Netlify read the netlify.toml in the BASE directory
# instead, and a config that lost its redirects deployed a site whose front
# door answered 404 — verified in a browser, not guessed. A _redirects file
# travels in the publish directory itself, so it applies whichever config file
# ends up winning.
#
# Vite's root is the platform directory, so the entry is emitted at the path it
# occupies in the source tree. The dev server answers the front door with a
# middleware; a static host cannot run middleware, so it does the same with a
# rewrite. 200, not 301: the address stays the one the visitor typed.
/                 /apps/patient/web/index.html   200

# One page, one entry. The app owns its own navigation and reads nothing from
# the URL; the mock answers /v1/ inside the page, so nothing needs to escape.
/*                /apps/patient/web/index.html   200
